-All people have cursed energy that is emitted through emotions, jjk sorcerers can use cursed energy (if pet dies, increase energy)


-Cursed Energy reinforcement, increase speed, attack strength, and durability by covering body with energy, maybe do with a street fighter key combo system and the faster you do it the better

Cursed Energy reserves, trigered once when a player joins and saved to that player forever, it is the amount of cursed energy the person has,
you can store cursed energy in things like machines (like mechimaru) and use that to increase curse energy reserves

Cursed output is how much cursed energy you put into an attack (maybe control with scroll wheel) with each person having diffrent maxes that they call out (in chat)

Reversed curse Technique:
increasing cursed output is addition while making reversed cursed energy requires multiplication.
multiplication takes a ton more cursed energy
Reverse Cursed energy can be used to heal yourself and if your really good, to heal others
by putting in Reversed Curse Energy into a bad dude it takes a lot of damage
By putting Reversed Curse Technique into a Technique it does the opposite of what it is supposed to do

Domains:
Everyone has an innate domain that represents their soul

Six eyes makes good efficiency


Key.CursedEnergyMode -> enables all abilities to use cursed energy based on reserves.value
Key.IncreaseOutput (ScrollUp) -> increases output of all cursed energies, if maxed out, player types max output in chat (exponetial cost increase and exponential output increase)
Key.ReveresedEnergyMode -> enables all abilities to use reversed cursed energy if possible

Keybind one pressed -> nextKeybind.waitFor()
Combo.Attack1 -> first attack
Limitless ex: blue        reverse ex: red
Combo.Attack2 -> second attack
Shikigami ex: frog
Combo.Attack3 -> third attack
Shikigami ex: bird
Combo.Attack4 -> fourth attack
Shikigami ex: mahoraga
certin abilities have more combo's and expansion techniques are incredibly hard to setup (techniques that are completely unique and break the rules of the technique)

Key.inate -> enable constantly on ability
ex: lava guy makes all things around super hot fire (based on cursed energy)

Key.useEnergy ->
if normal defend/speed/attack increase
if reverse heal

Key.domain -> domain if possible (inate domain if not)
Key.simple-domain -> simple domain that based on player training

concentration -> increase when standing still or hit black flash


Combo:
client sends key hits -> server recieves (subtracts latency from the time)
each time server recieves, all combo keys of that type turn to ComboKey.keydown=true;

Devlog notes:
I had some problems with the server tick, basically in order to add something to the game timer, you need to call a registry function which adds it to the end of the "tick" (20 ticks per second)
The issue is, if I were to reset player information before the tick, then that information can't be used. the theoriatically sollution is to simply call register(player) before calling reset() but
what if a player decides to join/leave. how would one handle that?

Spent multiple days dealing with a bug that turned out to just be an issue with how I named an identifier (i used upercase letters when they weren't allowed)